e><lpage>3322</lpage><!--PubMed citation query: 'J Clin Oncol||16|3316||bib6|'--><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">9779707</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib7"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Curran</surname><given-names>WJ</given-names></name><name><surname>Scott</surname><given-names>CB</given-names></name><name><surname>Langer</surname><given-names>CJ</given-names></name><name><surname>Komaki</surname><given-names>R</given-names></name><name><surname>Lee</surname><given-names>JS</given-names></name><name><surname>Hauser</surname><given-names>S</given-names></name><name><surname>Movsas</surname><given-names>B</given-names></name><name><surname>Wasserman</surname><given-names>T</given-names></name><name><surname>Sause</surname><given-names>W</given-names></name><name><surname>Cox</surname><given-names>JD</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Long-term benefit is observed in a phase III comparison of sequential <italic>vs</italic> concurrent chemo-radiation for patients with unresected stage III NSCLC: RTOG 9410</article-title><source>Proc Am Soc Clin Oncol</source><year>2003</year><volume>22</volume>abstract no. 2499a</citation></ref><ref id="bib8"><citation citation-type="other"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Endo</surname><given-names>M</given-names></name><name><surname>Yamamoto</surname><given-names>N</given-names></name><name><surname>Sakai</surname><given-names>H</given-names></name><name><surname>Kubota</surname><given-names>K</given-names></name><name><surname>Kunitoh</surname><given-names>H</given-names></name><name><surname>Nakagawa</surname><given-names>K</given-names></name><name><surname>Takeda</surname><given-names>K</given-names></name><name><surname>Ichinose</surname><given-names>Y</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Phase II study of 3-weekly S-1 plus cisplatin in patients with advanced non-small cell lung cancer (NSCLC)</article-title><source>P